INT. OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - CUBICLE 14C - DAY

Grey carpet tiles. Grey partitions. A ficus, plastic, gathering dust on a filing cabinet. A motivational poster: PERSEVERE, with a kayaker in a flooded canyon.

NORBERT PLUM (50s, short-sleeved dress shirt, lanyard overlong) types with two fingers. He hasn't smiled since 2011.

IMOGEN TRAVIS-OKORO (20s, new hire, cardigan with a sticker still on the sleeve) appears at the cubicle opening with a box of donuts.

IMOGEN
Hi! I'm Imogen. I'm in 14D.

Norbert doesn't look up.

NORBERT
There's no 14D.

IMOGEN
They built it this morning.

NORBERT
Hm.

She sets the box on his desk. He finally looks at it. Then at her. Then, very slowly, he opens the lid and takes a donut.

NORBERT (CONT'D)
Thank you.

IMOGEN
You're welcome!

He bites. His eyes close. A tear slides from one of them.

IMOGEN (CONT'D)
Are you okay?

NORBERT
Fourteen years. Nobody has ever brought me a donut.

He wipes his face with the lanyard. She pulls over a chair and sits.
